============================================================
PART 3: STRUCTURAL ANALYSIS — ODD CYCLE TRIPLES
============================================================

At n=5: detailed analysis of tournaments with alpha_1=3
  alpha_1=3 is IMPOSSIBLE at n=5!
  This is the fundamental reason H=7 is impossible at n=5.

  Proof sketch: In any n=5 tournament, the number of odd cycles
  jumps from 2 to 4 (never equals 3).
  Why? Every pair of odd cycles in a 5-vertex tournament that intersect
  forces the existence of additional odd cycles.

